{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"laplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"smallest"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"maxIterations"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ, relative to itself as for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"algebraicConnectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when given, is at least 1."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" products","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Throws"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/laplacianeigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxiterations:)"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"laplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"smallest"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs.swift#L332","fileName":"Eigenpairs.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE19laplacianEigenpairs8smallest9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0F0VyxGSi_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"laplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)"},"abstract":[{"text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the Laplacian L (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianMatrix()"},{"text":"), k = ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Eigenpairs"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/laplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Sp